{"rule": "When one group is described as flouting the law by crossing on the red signal, it picks the option that kills the red-signal group.", "members": ["H0000"]},
{"rule": "When the choice is car passengers (concrete barrier) versus pedestrians who are not described as crossing on red, it picks the option that crashes into the barrier and kills the passengers, regardless of demographics, status or numbers.", "members": ["H0001"]},
{"rule": "When both groups are pedestrians in two lanes and no signal colour is given, it picks the option that continues ahead rather than swerving.", "members": ["H0002"]},
{"rule": "When both groups are pedestrians with no legal status and differ in size, it picks the option that kills fewer people, even if that requires swerving.", "members": ["H0003"]},
{"rule": "When one side consists only of animals and the other of humans, it picks the option that kills the animals and spares the humans.", "members": ["H0004"]},
{"rule": "When passengers including children face adult or elderly pedestrians with no signal information, it picks the option that spares the children in the car and kills the pedestrians.", "members": ["H0005"]}
]}
